PS5: keep the full GPU reset off by default

From the official ps5-linux-patches, b33e7c5 (#81), "ps5: keep the full gpu reset off by default":

  the recovery check returns early on gpus without ras, so the existing cyan skillfish exclusion is never reached on
  ps5. check the ps5 default before that return. per queue recovery stays on, and a failed queue reset no longer falls
  through to the full reset, which does not work on ps5. explicit gpu_recovery=1 and other gpus are unchanged.

  tested with gpu hangs on a ps5: queue resets cleared every hang without a full reset and kept the desktop, a failed
  queue reset stopped recovery instead of escalating, and the next ring reset recovered the gpu

Seen here on a PS5 Pro (BeamNG.drive through vkd3d, 15 November): "Ring gfx_0.0.0 reset failed", then "MODE1 reset",
"ring kiq_0.2.1.0 test failed (-110)", "GPU Recovery Failed: -110", and the display stopped (pageflip timeouts) until a
restart. The same five lines, which apply to rmux's tree unchanged; amdgpu_device.o compiles.
---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_device.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_device.c
index 52ab4c8d7..c149165a0 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_device.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_device.c
@@ -4933,6 +4933,12 @@ bool amdgpu_device_should_recover_gpu(struct amdgpu_device *adev)
 	if (amdgpu_gpu_recovery == 0)
 		goto disabled;
 
+#ifdef CONFIG_X86_PS5
+	/* No PSP/SMU reset on PS5; only per-queue reset works. */
+	if (amdgpu_gpu_recovery == -1 && adev->asic_type == CHIP_CYAN_SKILLFISH)
+		goto disabled;
+#endif
+
 	/* Skip soft reset check in fatal error mode */
 	if (!amdgpu_ras_is_poison_mode_supported(adev))
 		return true;
